    "id": "cf11a257ed947022731247a8",
    "path": "parquet_variant::builder::metadata::ReadOnlyMetadataBuilder",
    "name": "ReadOnlyMetadataBuilder",
    "owner": null,
    "crate": "parquet-variant",
    "version": "59.3.0",
    "kind": "struct",
    "signature": "struct ReadOnlyMetadataBuilder<'m>",
    "docs": "A metadata builder that cannot register new field names, and merely returns the field id\nassociated with a known field name. This is useful for variant unshredding operations, where the\nmetadata column is fixed and -- per variant shredding spec -- already contains all field names\nfrom the typed_value column. It is also useful when projecting a subset of fields from a variant\nobject value, since the bytes can be copied across directly without re-encoding their field ids.\n\nNOTE: [`Self::finish`] is a no-op. If the intent is to make a copy of the underlying bytes each\ntime `finish` is called, a different trait impl will be needed.",
